      "Because the route to the bone is mapped in advance, the surgery is more controlled and typically less invasive than conventional placement. The guide allows smaller, more precise access, which often means less swelling, less bleeding, and a smoother recovery. Just as importantly, planning around critical structures such as the inferior alveolar nerve and the maxillary sinus is safer when every millimetre is verified digitally beforehand. This precision also sets the foundation for a better-fitting, more natural final crown or bridge, because the implant sits exactly where the restoration needs it.",
      "What makes Dental Med Austria's version premium is the combination of premium-quality protocols, modern CBCT imaging, and digital guide technology used as standard rather than as an upsell. International patients receive a free remote treatment plan within 24-48 hours, so much of the planning is completed before you travel, keeping your time in Tirana focused and efficient. From your first scan to your final restoration, the same precise digital blueprint guides every step, giving you confidence that nothing is left to guesswork."
