  "cbct-scan": {
    "description": "Low-dose Vatech A9 CBCT 3D dental imaging in Tirana, Albania - precise jaw, nerve and sinus mapping for safe implant, All-on-X and complex surgical planning.",
    "intro": "A CBCT 3D scan captures a detailed three-dimensional map of your jaw, teeth, nerves and sinuses with low-dose Vatech A9 technology - the foundation for planning implants, All-on-X and complex surgery with precision and safety.",
    "details": [
      "Cone-beam computed tomography (CBCT) rotates a single time around your head to reconstruct a true three-dimensional model of your jawbone, tooth roots, nerve canals and sinus cavities - detail that is simply impossible to see on a flat, two-dimensional X-ray. At Dental Med Austria we use the Vatech A9 CBCT, a modern low-dose system that delivers sharp diagnostic images while keeping radiation exposure to a minimum. The scan itself is quick, completely painless and requires nothing more than sitting or standing still for a few seconds. From that single capture, your clinician can measure bone volume and density, locate the inferior alveolar nerve and map the sinus floor down to the millimetre.",
      "This 3D data is what turns implant and full-arch treatment from guesswork into a precisely engineered plan. By seeing exactly where there is enough healthy bone - and exactly where critical nerves and sinuses sit - your surgeon can choose the right implant length, angle and position before any procedure begins, which reduces surprises and improves both safety and the final result. The same imaging is invaluable for diagnosing impacted wisdom teeth, hidden infections, jaw pathology and the airway, and for planning bone grafts or sinus lifts. It is a core part of how we plan All-on-X and other complex cases with confidence.",
      "What makes CBCT at Dental Med Austria premium is how the scan is read and used, not just the hardware. Your Vatech A9 images are interpreted by our experienced clinical team and integrated directly into your personalised treatment plan, so every recommendation is grounded in real anatomy rather than assumption. For international patients, this 3D data also powers our free remote treatment plan: a recent CBCT can be reviewed before you ever board a flight, allowing us to outline your options, timeline and the scope of work in advance so your time in Tirana is spent efficiently and predictably."
    ],
    "benefits": [
      "Detailed 3D view of bone, nerves and sinuses for precise planning",
      "Low-dose Vatech A9 CBCT imaging with minimal radiation",
      "Essential for safe implant, All-on-X and surgical care",
      "Fast, painless scan completed in seconds",
      "Powers a free remote treatment plan for international patients"
    ],
    "idealFor": "Patients planning dental implants, All-on-X or complex oral surgery - and international patients who want their case assessed accurately before travelling.",
    "aftercare": "There is no recovery or downtime - you can return to normal activities immediately. Your 3D images are reviewed by our team and built into your treatment plan, and we are happy to share the findings with you and explain the next steps.",
    "duration": "5-10 minutes (single visit)",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Is a CBCT scan safe?",
        "a": "Yes - the Vatech A9 uses a low radiation dose and provides information impossible to see on a standard X-ray, improving both the safety and accuracy of your treatment."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do I need a CBCT for implants?",
        "a": "For implant and full-arch planning it is strongly recommended, as it reveals bone volume and density and the exact position of nerves and sinuses, which is essential for placing implants safely."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does the scan hurt and how long does it take?",
        "a": "Not at all - it is completely painless. You simply stay still for a few seconds while the scanner rotates once around your head, and the whole appointment takes only minutes."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can you review my CBCT before I travel to Tirana?",
        "a": "Yes. If you have a recent CBCT, we can review it remotely and prepare a free treatment plan with your options and timeline before you book your trip."
      },
      {
        "q": "What can a CBCT show beyond implants?",
        "a": "Besides implant planning, it helps diagnose impacted wisdom teeth, hidden infections, jaw pathology, sinus issues and bone grafting needs, giving a complete picture of your oral health."
      }
    ]
  },
