    "details": [
      "At its heart is a precision-cast chrome-cobalt (cobalt-chromium) alloy core, milled and finished to fit your prepared tooth exactly. Over this metal substructure our technicians hand-apply and fire layers of layered ceramic, which is shade-matched to your neighbouring teeth so the finished crown reads as a natural white tooth. The metal gives the restoration its backbone - excellent rigidity and a tight marginal seal - while the ceramic provides the lifelike outer surface. The result is a time-tested metal-ceramic crown that has restored chewing function reliably for decades.",
      "Chrome-cobalt is fully biocompatible and contains no nickel, so it sits comfortably against the gum without the sensitivity some patients have to other alloys. Because the alloy is so strong, the crown stands up to the heavy, repeated loads of the molar and premolar region better than many thinner all-ceramic options, making it a sensible, dependable choice where strength matters most. The ceramic layer is built up by hand rather than simply pressed, allowing our ceramist to control colour and contour for a result that blends in rather than stands out. For most cases it is completed comfortably within one to two visits.",
      "What makes the Dental Med Austria version premium is the discipline behind it: rigorous clinical protocols, a precise digital and analogue fit, and ceramic layered by an experienced lab team rather than rushed. International patients receive a free written treatment plan within 24-48 hours of sending a panoramic X-ray and a few photos, so you know exactly what is proposed and why before you ever travel. Every fact about your case - the tooth, the bite, the materials - is reviewed individually so the crown is built for your mouth, not a template."
    ],
    "benefits": [
      "Tough cobalt-chromium core built for heavy chewing loads on back teeth",
      "Nickel-free and fully biocompatible, kind to the surrounding gums",
      "Precise, well-sealing fit that protects the prepared tooth beneath",
      "Hand-layered ceramic shade-matched to a natural white tooth",
      "Proven, dependable metal-ceramic restoration with a long clinical track record"
    ],
    "idealFor": "Patients restoring a molar or premolar who want proven strength and reliable, long-lasting function.",
    "aftercare": "There is little downtime - any mild sensitivity around the prepared tooth settles within a few days, and the crown can be used for normal eating almost immediately. Keep it healthy with routine brushing, flossing or interdental cleaning around the margin, and regular check-ups, just as you would a natural tooth.",
