      "Every retained extraction begins with a careful assessment of how deeply the tooth sits and how close it lies to nerves, sinuses, and the roots beside it - which is exactly why we read your panoramic X-ray before we ever pick up an instrument. By planning the access route in advance, our surgeons remove the tooth with the least possible disturbance to the gum and jawbone, which is what keeps swelling down and recovery quick. You stay fully numb the entire time, and we walk you through each step so there are no surprises.",
